# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# starwatch worker — local/deploy environment
# Copy to `.env` in this directory (apps/worker/.env). Alchemy loads it
# automatically for `plan | deploy | dev`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ── Cloudflare credentials ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Option A — headless/CI (recommended for deploy):
#   Create a token at https://dash.cloudflare.com/profile/api-tokens
#   using the "Edit Cloudflare Workers" template, then add D1 (Edit) and
#   R2 (Edit) permissions. Account ID is on the dashboard overview page.
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=

# Option B — interactive (recommended for local):
#   pnpm --filter @starwatch/worker exec alchemy profile create default
#   pnpm --filter @starwatch/worker exec alchemy profile edit
#   ...then leave the two variables above empty.

# ── GitHub (strongly recommended; required for collections) ───────────────
# Fine-grained PAT with public read only. Two reasons to always set it:
#   1. GitHub's GraphQL API — the only API with the public Lists that become
#      collections — requires authentication. Empty = anonymous: stars still
#      index, but the Lists step is skipped and the rail says so.
#   2. The REST quota goes from 60 requests/hour (anonymous, shared per IP) to
#      5,000/hour, which a 3.4k-star listing needs.
# This value is also bound to the Worker as a secret at deploy time.
GITHUB_TOKEN=
